(a) the total number of Compressed Biogas (CBG) plants established under the Sustainable Alternative Towards Affordable Transportation (SATAT) Scheme out of the 5,000 target set in 2018 to be achieved by 2023-24, especially in Telangana;
(b) the district-wise data of Telangana;
(c) whether Government is taking steps to promote the establishment of CBG plants in the State of Telangana; and
(d) if the target has not been met, the reasons therefor?

(a) whether Government has information regarding Tesla’s intention to set up EV manufacturing in India;
(b) if so, which States are being considered for this remarkable revolutionary project that will boost a State’s economic prowess;
(c) whether Telangana is being prioritised by Government as it invites other global giants to expand its business in India; and
(d) if so, any updates of any discussion/deals with stakeholders that could turn into potential projects?
BS

(a) the extent to which the National Electric Mobility Mission Plan (NEMMP) has been successful in upgrading technology, enhancing competitiveness and generating employment therefrom; 
(b) the kind of investments Government received with respect to the Plan; and
(c) the manner in which the implementation of the Mission Plan has benefited the country in the global trade?

(a) whether the telecom companies are disseminating obscene, misleading and undesired advertisements through e-mail, WhatsApp messenger, Facebook, etc., for their financial benefit;
(b) if so, the details of the complaints received in this regard;
(c) whether the said disseminated messages are against the traditions of Indian culture and society, which are adversely affecting the young generations; and
(d) if so, the effective steps proposed to be taken to check the dissemination of the said messages?

(a) the details of unprotected heritage monuments/sites in various parts of the State of Telangana;
(b) whether Government provides funds for maintenance of unprotected heritage structures/ monuments in the country; and
(c) if so, the details thereof during each of the last three years and the current year for Telangana and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of funds allotted and utilised under the National Health Mission (NHM) since its inception, in Telangana;
(b) whether Government has taken/proposes to take any steps to allocate more funds to strengthen the National Health Mission and make it more effective;
(c) if so, the details thereof, and if not, the reasons therefor;
(d) the details of Community Health Centres (CHCs) and Public Health Centres (PHCs) established under NHM since its inception in Telangana; and
(e) the steps taken by Government to assess the implementation and progress of NHM, along with its present status?
D

(a) the number of beneficiaries in various categories of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) under Emergency Credit Line Guarantee Scheme (ECLGS), State-wise;
(b) whether eligible and COVID-19 affected MSMEs in Telangana have been provided incentive under ECLGS and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the number of MSMEs owners from Telangana who are selling properties to regularise their current loans and to make re-investment in their business?

(a) whether Government provides any assistance to the farmers during natural calamities;
(b) the norms and rules of procedure to get assistance and relief work to farmers of the States during natural calamities; and
(c) if so, the details thereof along with the assistance provided to Telangana during the last three year in this regard?

(a) whether Government has contemplated on shortage of Courtrooms, residential quarters for district and subordinate judiciary in the State of Telangana;
(b) if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the constraints, if any, being faced by Government to help the State Government in dealing with infrastructural challenges being faced by lower judiciary and the steps taken to address the same?

(a) the steps taken by Government for formalisation of sanitation workers in informal sector;
(b) whether Government is collecting data regarding the number of sanitation workers and the ones working in high risk conditions; and
(c) if so, the details thereof including for Telangana and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of the sanctioned posts, filled up posts, shortfall and backlog vacancies as on 18.10.22 in various hospitals and Central institutes of medicine under the Central Government, including AllMS, category-wise;
(b) whether Government has conducted any review meeting at the Central level to look at the reasons for such shortfall and backlog vacancies for filling up the vacancies through a time-bound method of recruitment, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) the time by when such backlog vacancies of reserved category are likely to be filled up?

(a) the details of funds transferred to Telangana under different Centrally Sponsored Schemes (CSS) during the last three years and the current year, head-wise and department-wise;
(b) whether the Union Government has received any representation from the Government of Telangana for more fund allocations to the State for various developmental works, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) whether the Union Government has taken steps to grant more funds to Telangana for taking up developmental activities, if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Railways have has taken any decision to upgrade railway stations in Telangana in view of tourism and commercial importance; 
(b) if so, the details thereof and the present status in this regard; and
(c) the details of developers who have shown keenness to redevelop these railway stations?

(a) whether a large number of projects were pending with the Union Government since long for want of environmental clearance; 
(b) if so, the details thereof, State/UT-wise and the reasons for such undue delay particularly in the State of Telangana;
(c) whether Government/National Board of Wildlife (NBWL) have cleared number of pending proposals including the projects on habitation/adjoining areas of endangered animals; and 
(d) if so, the details thereof and the steps taken by Government to protect fauna and flora and the depleting forest cover in the country?

(a) details of the roads in each district of Telangana that are being covered for financial assistance under Central Road Fund (CRF)/ Central Road and Infrastructure Fund (CRIF) at present;
(b) whether the funds have been released for the said roads and if so, the details thereof; and
(c) if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the details of grants released to State of Telangana under various schemes of the Ministry during each of the last three years;
(b) whether the said grants were released on time during the said period;
(c) if so, the details thereof along with the grants released so far, scheme-wise and year-wise; and
(d) the details of utilisation of the said grant/expenditure incurred during the said period, sector-wise?
